{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Implementation landed for review as Gerrit change 1818 (https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/1818), commit 8b05e976fa, worktree locust-autoresume.\n\nWhat was built (exactly the v6 design):\n- NEW src/rebar/_commands/close_autoresume.py: verify_with_auto_resume — the bounded resumption loop, extracted as a helper along the existing call seam so _completion_precheck stays at its frozen complexity ceiling and close_precheck.py under the 800-LOC cap. close_precheck._completion_precheck's llm.verify_completion call site now calls the helper (the ONE seam shared by CLI/MCP/library via transition_close.close_ticket); gate_dispatch/CompletionAgentStep untouched.\n- Qualification REUSES completion_reconcile._insufficiency_only unchanged (asserted by a counting-wrapper test); no schema/prompt/model-facing changes.\n- Bounds: new verify.auto_resume_max config key (default 2; 0 disables; _as_int minimum=0; documented in docs/config.md) AND strict progress — a resumption dispatches only while the prior attempt strictly increased the cache-credited PASS count (seeded:true + met:true criteria records); zero progress stops early.\n- Trail: per attempt {attempt, cache_credited, remaining_unmet} attached to the verdict when a resumption ran (single-attempt verdicts keep their exact prior shape), carried onto the durable COMPLETION_VERDICT sidecar (both PASS and FAIL branches of build_payload), and the refusal message states the resumption count + per-attempt counts.\n- Tests: tests/unit/test_close_autoresume_b5f8.py (17) — insufficiency-only resumes / refutation fails fast / plain PASS / zero-unmet FAIL, predicate reuse, max bound + attempts-count message, 0 disables, unchanged-count early stop, progress-then-stall = exactly one extra attempt, same pinned --ref on every attempt, trail on emitted FAIL sidecar + resumed PASS, config default/coercion, and a library-path close (rebar.transition -> close_ticket) exercising the shared seam.\n\nGates: make lint clean (complexity ratchet new=0 increased=0), make typecheck clean, full tests/unit green (10650 passed; pre-existing failures on this host were traced to harness-injected GIT_CONFIG safe.bareRepository=explicit, not the change — they pass with that env removed, on main too).\n\nAlso: file_impact refreshed to the actually-touched paths (the previously recorded workflow/completion_* paths were from a superseded plan revision; the v6 description's close_precheck seam is what landed). Frontier-handoff out-of-scope work parked as idea ticket daemonic-rounded-gnu (e82c-dd27-e3e8-4bb5), linked discovered_from this ticket.\n\nNext: await LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1 on change 1818, Submit, then close this ticket."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786822069750301001,"uuid":"2ea41d74-ffb0-4a12-81e5-05d7609ec2df"}